+# N1 v2 receiver implementation report
+
+## Initial design/config freeze before development measurement
+
+This file and `receiver_config.json` define the v2 receiver before any v2 source or target measurement. The carrier remains exactly `n=1000`, `c=5`, `m=52500`, block 6, 144 DPI, strength 4.0, and original epsilon `1e-6`. The public synthetic fixture identifiers are test inputs, not production credentials.
+
+Preparation is recipient-blind. It may derive the implemented bias vector through a zero-roster call and may render the two all-zero/all-one carrier endpoints, but it may not generate or inspect a recipient row, labels, expected contributors, or verdict metadata. Source eligibility is selected solely from source luma: normalized gradients are stratified across a fixed spatial grid and four tone ranges. Eligibility requires support, spatial spread, tone diversity, full photometric rank, and a bounded condition number; a blank page is expected to be inconclusive. The previous absolute 4096-pixel cutoff is not retained.
+
+Accepted registration is a hard gate. Geometry uses only visible source content and the capture; an injected transform is never treated as registration evidence. A single global blur and bounded robust photometric fit are shared by global and local evidence. Local evidence uses the same calibration data, fixed subpixel candidates, content-only losses, and uncertainty marginalization. It never optimizes a warp against a recipient.
+
+Each usable profile commits candidate-independent channel components plus per-symbol `q_j(0)` and `q_j(1)` log evidence. Erased or insufficient symbols have both values exactly zero. The compound scorer uses one implementation for global and local evidence. Average attacks integrate the rendered endpoint interpolation over the specified binomial latent count; interleaving uses the specified contributor-conditioned mixture. Soft hypothesis keys are exactly `single`, `average_2`, `average_5`, and `interleave_5`; the calibrated hard key is `hard`. Scores use a fixed positive Chernoff grid under the conditional implemented-Bernoulli row model. The result is a numerical conditional-model calculation, not empirical certification of a `1e-6` physical false-attribution rate.
+
+This section records the prospective starting point committed before development measurements. It is not a final model freeze. The first development run exposed effectively absent local coverage, and the authorized, target-row-blind correction is recorded below. No new physical capture or confirmation set was opened.
