+### Assumptions, deviations, and open concerns
+
+- All evidence here is synthetic/digital development evidence. It establishes executable software and separation on the declared matrix, not physical readiness or N1 research success.
+- The public fixture seed and context are reproducibility inputs, not private keys or production credential handling.
+- The initial sparse-local interpretation was corrected before confirmation because it gave `0/234` coverage. The final implementation should receive independent review before any validation/final freeze.
+- Global blur is selected once; local translation uncertainty is conditional on it. Blur uncertainty is not marginalized.
+- Local coverage is still low and content-dependent: the preserved round-0 table result was `4/234`, and the corrected content-only final matrix is `3/234`. The explicit global fallback dominates many pages.
+- Local had no accusation-set improvement over global on the development matrix. No performance gain is claimed.
+- Fit correlation and inferred-coordinate correlation are recipient-blind fit diagnostics, not carrier BER/survival. Actual evaluator-labelled amplitude and BER remain pending the evaluation worker and real captures.
+- Chernoff thresholds are conditional on the implemented independent-Bernoulli row model and fixed numerical grid. They do not empirically certify a `1e-6` real-world false-attribution probability.
+- The transplant recovered a donor pattern, which is explicitly not authenticity, culpability, or security success.
+- Negative scores and thresholds are expected because a common per-symbol maximum is subtracted from `q0/q1`; only the strict score-versus-threshold comparison is meaningful.
+- No human-culpability conclusion is emitted anywhere in the API.
+
+## Independent-review fix round 1
+
+The independent review at `task-1-review-report.md` found three important boundary defects. Commit `7db5df2ad05280f668d808faed4bf05ab4b553c3` fixes all three without changing carrier parameters, profile/hypothesis keys, calibration thresholds, or physical-study claims.
+
+### Corrected content-only local fit
+
+Round 0 used `reference_expectation`, constructed from rendered endpoints and implemented biases, when fitting each local shift's gain, offset, residual loss, noise, and posterior. That contradicted the stated content-only warp boundary. The final implementation instead blurs `source_luma` with the already globally selected sigma, fits each fixed shift against that content reference, and freezes those gains, offsets, losses, noises, and posterior weights before applying them to the blurred endpoint likelihood coordinates. Endpoint/bias descriptors cannot affect `log_weights`.
+
+The global blur remains a single selected value, and local translation uncertainty remains conditional on it. Blur uncertainty is still not marginalized. No blur grid, support bound, strength, payload, Chernoff grid, or physical threshold was retuned.
+
+The focused regression holds source, capture, support, and the global fallback fixed while replacing both endpoints and their bias-weighted expectation. Before the fix all 2,304 log-weight entries changed; after the fix the arrays are exactly equal. The serialized diagnostic now states `local_photometric_reference="blurred source_luma; endpoint and bias descriptors are excluded"`.
+
+### Strict request and provenance boundaries
+
+The top-level request is now an exact allowlist of `schema`, `request_id`, `source_pdf`, `source_sha256`, `capture_path`, `capture_sha256`, `context`, `carrier`, and `receiver_config_path`. Evaluator-only `attack`, top-level sheet `kind`, and arbitrary unknown extras are rejected. Required nested `context.kind="public_fixture_v1"` remains valid. The existing recursive evaluator-field rejection remains in force, with `attack` added to it.
+
+The implementation map now contains exactly the eight directly used project files required by the corrected binding specification, adding `prototypes/nishan_pq/nishan/watermark.py`. This binds the PDF validation/rendering and luma code as well as the receiver, channel, scorer, config, code generator, carrier, and registration modules. Installed-library versions remain separately recorded and are not represented as project-file hashes.
+
