+## Same-size cross-renderer registration repair
+
+The integrated approved calibration pack exposed a real pre-confirmation software defect after review round 1. MuPDF renders the retained source reference, while the approved A1 integration probe used a Poppler render of the marked sheet. Both rasters were exactly `1190 x 1684`, but their rasterizer/resampling differences put the gradient similarity below the unchanged identity guard. `registration.align_page` then proposed an ORB homography which made the content metric worse. The v2 wrapper immediately propagated that rejection, so its existing ECC refinement was never reached. For A1 the rejected diagnostics were baseline `0.892264`, ORB candidate `0.757315`, and 270/455 RANSAC inliers. This was a registration-control-flow failure before channel fitting, not evidence that the carrier was absent.
+
+Commits `019b4a2a3b23f68c2b69763512394e7022f8086a` (RED tests) and `9b0d01a995af7fd1e55e3945150b8e80f77705b8` (repair) add one v2-only retry. The shared v1 registration module and every calibration PDF byte remain unchanged. When, and only when, the legacy content path rejects an exact-same-size raster, the wrapper starts an identity-initialized ECC affine fit from visible source and capture pixels. It inverse-maps that affine and resamples the original capture once. It never uses a Tardos row, expected contributor, evaluator label, decoded bit, or target score. Both global and local evidence consume the resulting single aligned raster.
+
+The original `same_geometry_similarity_guard=0.92` is unchanged. The retry is not a lower identity threshold and is not accepted merely because ECC returns a matrix. Every frozen condition must pass:
+
+| Criterion | Frozen development bound |
+|---|---:|
+| exact raster geometry | required |
+| ECC content correlation | at least `0.5` |
+| affine 2x2 condition number | at most `1.01` |
+| maximum singular-value deviation from 1 | at most `0.01` |
+| translation norm | at most `2.0 px` |
+| transformed support overlap | at least `0.995` |
+| source-defined support | at least `4096` pixels and rank 2 |
+| registered normalized source-content RMSE | at most `0.75` |
+| normalized RMSE improvement | at least `0.005` |
+| existing registered-similarity floor | at least `0.08` |
+
+The residual check blurs source and capture luma by sigma `1.5`, builds support only from source ink below `0.985` or source Sobel magnitude above `0.01`, dilates that support by 5 pixels, and fits only gain/offset on those fixed positions. The accepted transform also preserves orientation and must be finite. The diagnostic records every bound, criterion result, source-content fit rank/condition, discarded ORB proposal, accepted raw-to-reference matrix, and the statement `visible source and capture content only; no carrier bits or recipient rows`.
+
+These values are a disclosed **digital development configuration change before physical confirmation**. They were chosen after comparing the approved A/B Poppler/MuPDF calibration renderings with crossed A/B wrong-source controls. They were not fit to expected rows, evaluator BER, accusation sets, or the newly supplied physical photographs. The physical photographs were not opened or used in this repair. No watermark strength, code length, block size, payload, source-support rule, global blur grid, local shift grid, evidence variance, Chernoff grid, or accusation threshold changed.
