+# Unchanged-carrier receiver pilot — measured report
+
+Date: 16 September 2026. Branch: `research/robustness-20260916-receiver`.
+Protected demo baseline: `f37e861dc02815adf1bebb3e1b45ff222dccf821` (not modified).
+
+## Result first
+
+The frozen soft-receiver proposal did **not** produce a valid broad comparison. The historical hard extractor prepared 16 of 20 frozen cases and, under its matched conditional Chernoff boundary, returned 12 correct row-pattern outcomes, four abstentions, no wrong row, and four retained input/registration failures. One of the 12 is the copied-overlay transplant and is not a security success. Excluding that known transplant, the hard profile produced 11 correct outcomes and four abstentions among 15 scored cases.
+
+Each signed-soft profile prepared only two cases: `sourcepack_dev_table_global` and the known transplant. Each had 18 retained failures (14 at the frozen 4,096-content-pixel gate, three at registration, and the sealed prospective input). The sole non-transplant matched case selected row 0 under all three profiles, so there is no success-count improvement to claim. On that case the global-soft profile was also better than the local mixture on both sign BER (0.041676 versus 0.064743) and expected-row margin (27,723.075 versus 26,455.688). The preregistered hypothesis that this local mixture helps under spatially varying registration is therefore not supported by this bounded run.
+
+This is a negative implementation result, not evidence that soft decoding in general is ineffective. Soft Tardos decoding and synchronization/channel fitting are established directions in the cited literature. Here, the particular frozen content-mask eligibility rule was incompatible with most tested pages.
+
+The reserved prospective camera/transfer-unknown capture also produced **no recovery**. The hard profile ran, ranked row 0 first, but scored `923.890`, below its unchanged conditional threshold `1142.690` (margin `-218.800`), and accused nobody. Both soft profiles failed the same frozen content gate before scoring. This one-time result is an abstention, not attribution and not evidence of physical robustness.
+
+## Matched outcomes
+
+All profiles used identical embedded bytes at `n=1000`, `c=5`, `m=52500`, 6-pixel blocks, 144 DPI, and strength 4. Preparation used no recipient rows or labels. Scoring generated the roster only after the two-file preparation commitment had been committed.
+
+| Profile | Prepared/scored | Correct pattern | Abstain | Wrong | Failure |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| Hard, conditional matched boundary | 16/20 | 12 | 4 | 0 | 4 |
+| Global signed-soft | 2/20 | 2 | 0 | 0 | 18 |
+| Local-mixture signed-soft | 2/20 | 2 | 0 | 0 | 18 |
+
+The table reports actual decoder pattern outcomes. It includes one known transplant as a recovered donor pattern in each profile; those three records explicitly set `security_success_counted=false` and `deployable_manipulation_detected=false`.
+
+The unchanged historical `2100` cutoff was applied only to the hard asymmetric score. Among the 16 hard-scored cases it produced 10 correct pattern outcomes and six abstentions. The matched conditional hard boundary produced two additional recoveries: the synthetic white-clipping stress (`1374.907 > 310.045`) and historical `legacy-capture-3.jpeg` (`1709.941 > 1145.125`). No boundary was selected from a target score. Every conditional profile used strict `score > threshold`, family epsilon `10^-6`, and the preregistered `H=60,000`, including failed and reserved hypotheses.
+
+### Physical development captures
+
+These four files were repeatedly examined historical development inputs, not unseen confirmation.
+
+| Capture category | Row-0 score | Conditional threshold | Rank | Conditional outcome | Historical 2100 |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---|---|
+| Scanner/enhancement (`legacy-capture-0.jpeg`) | 66.070 | 432.615 | 146 | abstain | abstain |
+| WhatsApp ordinary photo (`legacy-capture-1.jpeg`) | -11.627 | 461.870 | 544 | abstain | abstain |
+| Ordinary photo, transfer unknown (`legacy-capture-2.jpeg`) | 788.315 | 1065.517 | 1 | abstain | abstain |
+| Real-camera JPEG (`legacy-capture-3.jpeg`) | 1709.941 | 1145.125 | 1 | row 0 only | abstain |
+
+The soft profiles did not score any historical capture because the existing source produced only 1,675 pixels under the frozen content-mask definition, below the fixed minimum of 4,096. The run did not lower that minimum after seeing the failure.
+
+## Controls and failure audit
+
+- The wrong-key hard control accused nobody. Its soft profiles failed the content gate.
+- The other-issued row-1 hard control selected row 1 only. Its soft profiles failed the content gate.
+- All three profiles recovered row 0 from the copied-overlay transplant. This shows donor-pattern copying, not source authenticity. The evaluator's safe disposition is abstention, but the runtime has no manipulation detector and cannot use the oracle fixture label; this is not counted as security success.
+- The unmarked and wrong-source controls failed the frozen same-size registration guard before scoring. They therefore do not provide usable negative-control accusation evidence. This incomplete control coverage prevents a broad receiver claim.
+- `sourcepack_validation_diagram_combined` failed the same registration guard in all three profiles.
